  "summary": "Photographic technique simulating miniature scenes through selective focus and perspective distortion.",
  "description": "Characterized by extreme selective focus with sharp center and blurred edges, often with exaggerated perspective; achieved by tilting the lens relative to the image sensor to manipulate the plane of focus. Popularized by architectural photographers for correcting perspective, later adopted as an artistic effect to make real scenes appear as miniatures.",
